remstart
    SCHOOLS
    another hidden thing, and a prototype. the routines are in fish_routines_school, and the tests are
    in fish_tests_school.

    FACING. every fish faces left or right. a new fish comes in facing one way or the other, picked by
    the seed and how many fish have come in so far, so a seed plays the same, and no roll is taken from
    the streams. a swap that goes across turns the two fish that it moves: the fish that the cursor
    carries faces the way that it was carried, and the fish that it shoves faces the other way. a swap
    that goes up or down leaves them facing the way that they were. a "free move" turns them the same as
    any swap does. the special moves do not. a fish takes the way that it faces along with it, when it
    is swapped or falls: swapCellStacks, in fish_funcs, trades it.
    the picture of a fish faces one way, and SCHOOL_ART_FACE says which. a fish that faces the other way
    is drawn turned around, and it turns slowly, so a swap that turns it can be seen. frame_fish_fx adds
    SCHOOL_SHOWN# to the yaw. a crab, a jellyfish, a stingray and a bottle look the same from either side,
    so the way that they face cannot be seen, and they are never in a school. crabs walk sideways anyway.

    A SCHOOL. a group of fish that matched is a school when all of these are so:
        none of its fish is a crab, or one of the others that look the same from either side. it can
            be any shape.
        every fish of it faces the same way
        it has SCHOOL_MIN fish, or more
        the swap that led to this look at the board put one of its two fish in it. a group that only
            fell together is never a school. SCHOOL_NEED_SWAP turns that off, for the debug panel.
    by chance, three fish would face the same way one time in four, and four of them one time in eight.
    the swap has to have made it so that it does not happen too often without the player meaning it to.

    A SCHOOL SWIMS OFF. a school does not pop. it scores the same as if it had, and it leaves the board
    the same way, but there is no puff and no bang: each of its fish fades off of the board as a fish
    just like it lifts off and swims away, slowly, the way that the school faced, out into the water
    behind the board. it gets smaller as it goes, as if it were going further away, a blue haze comes
    over it, and the dark line around it fades, the way that it would be lost in the water far off.
    FlockEffect.fx does the line. the bubbles still come up from where it was, and in place of the
    bang, a chord rings. schoolFishLeaves does the rest of it, from where handle_combos would have made
    the puff, and schoolChord the chord.

    THE FANFARE OF THE SCHOOLS. every school, of any kind, plays a short fanfare: a chord, rolled quickly
    from the bottom note up, with its root again an octave higher on top. a school of
    SCHOOL_FANFARE_BIG fish or more adds one more note, higher still. every school plays the next chord
    of a run of SCHOOL_FANFARE_LENGTH of them, and when SCHOOL_SONG_RESET_MS go by with no school, the
    run starts again from the first. it is played on SCHOOL_CHORD_INSTRUMENT.
    the music has a chord under it all of the time, D minor or B flat (see MUSIC_CHORD in fish_headers),
    and its tunes are written over that chord. so there are two runs, one of chords that sit well over
    D minor, and one of chords that sit well over B flat, and a school plays from whichever one goes
    with the chord that is up. that way it does not clash with the music, or with a tune that is
    playing. setup_school writes the two runs, in SCHOOL_FANFARE_ROOT. a chord is its root and every
    other note of the scale above it, and the notes are the ones in fish_headers. a new game, and a
    game that is loaded, start the run from the first chord.

    THE SCHOOLS IN THE BACKGROUND. the fish that have swum off stay, out in the water behind the board,
    and every one of them joins the others of its kind: a school of every kind of fish that has been
    made into one. they flock, the way that real fish do. every fish keeps a little way from the fish
    of its kind that are closest, swims the way that they swim, and keeps close to them, and it keeps
    well away from fish of any other kind, so the schools stay apart. a fish that is a long way from
    its school is drawn back to it. none of them leave the screen. they would rather not swim over the
    board: one that is over it is pushed toward the nearer side of it, gently, so one can be seen
    crossing behind the fish now and then, or be made to by the others, but it does not stay there.
    this is only to be looked at, for now.
    there are FLOCK_MAX of them at the most. when another one comes, the one that has been out there
    the longest goes. a new game starts with none. a fish turns around when it starts to swim the
    other way: it narrows to nothing and opens out again facing the other way, the way that the fish on
    the board turn. they are kept with the saved game: see THE SAVED GAME, below.
    the flock is worked out a few fish at a time, FLOCK_STEER_EACH of them on a frame, since every
    fish has to look at every other one. that is when a fish changes how fast it goes, and which way:
    for the rest of the time it just goes. they all move on every frame. this is slow work for the
    script, so a frame does as little for each fish as it can, and the sprite of a fish that is all
    the way out is only told where it is, and how far around it is turned while it turns.
    LATER: cards may change what a school does. one could make it swim off through the fish in its
    way, popping them, which is what SCHOOL_SWEEP does: in every row that the school has a fish in,
    every fish ahead of it, from its front in that row to the edge of the board, pops too, as one
    forced group for that row. it goes past the diver. see FORCED POPS in fish_headers: a school in
    a row takes FORCE_SCHOOL and the row. schoolJudge does it, where handle_combos shoots the stingrays.
    SCHOOL_SWEEP is 0, for now.

    THE SAVED GAME. the way that every fish on the board faces, and the fish out in the background, are
    kept with the saved game, from SCHOOL_PREF on. a game that
    was saved before any of this deals the fish a way to face, and has nobody out in the background.
    schoolSave and schoolLoad, which fish_routines_save calls.

    the "Schools" window of the debug panel (FISH_DEBUG) turns it off and on, sets how big a school has
    to be, and turns every fish one way, the other way, or back to the way that it was dealt.
remend

global SCHOOL_ON = 1 `0 turns the whole thing off
global SCHOOL_MIN = 3 `how many fish a school needs, at the least
global SCHOOL_NEED_SWAP = 1 `1 when only a group that the last swap put together can be a school
global FORCE_SCHOOL = 120 `the fish ahead of a school that swims off. the row is added to this. see FORCED POPS in fish_headers.

global dim SCHOOL_FACE(400) `which way the fish in every cell faces: 1 is to the right, and -1 to the left
global dim SCHOOL_SHOWN#(400) `how far around the fish in every cell is drawn, from 0, the way that its picture faces, to 1, turned around
global dim SCHOOL_ART_FACE(64) `which way the picture of every kind of fish faces: 1 to the right, -1 to the left, and 0 for one that looks the same from either side. setup_school fills it in.
global SCHOOL_SNAP = 1 `1 when every fish should be drawn facing its way right away, without turning. a new game does that.
global SCHOOL_TURN_STEP# = 0 `how much of the way a fish turns on this frame. stepSchool works it out.
global SCHOOL_TURN_EASE# = 0.008 `how much of the way it turns in a millisecond
global SCHOOL_LAST_MS = 0
global SCHOOL_SPAWNS = 0 `how many fish have come in this game. it goes into which way the next one faces.

` what has happened, for the debug panel
global SCHOOL_COUNT = 0 `how many schools have swum off in this game
global SCHOOL_LAST_SIZE = 0 `how many fish the last one had
global SCHOOL_LAST_SWEPT = 0 `and how many it popped on its way off
global dim SCHOOL_ROW_LEFT(64) `scratch, for schoolJudge: the leftmost fish of the group in every row, or -1 for none
global dim SCHOOL_ROW_RIGHT(64) `and the rightmost

global SCHOOL_SWEEP = 0 `1 when a school swims off through the fish in its way, popping them. see LATER, above.
global SCHOOL_JUDGED = -1 `the group that schoolJudge last found to be a school, or -1. handle_combos asks about it as it pops the group.

` THE SCHOOLS IN THE BACKGROUND
global FLOCK_MAX = 48 `how many fish there can be out there at once
global dim FLOCK_ON(48) `1 for a fish that is out there
global dim FLOCK_KIND(48) `the kind of fish that it is
global dim FLOCK_X#(48) `where it is, in pixels
global dim FLOCK_Y#(48)
global dim FLOCK_VX#(48) `how fast it is going, in pixels a second
global dim FLOCK_VY#(48)
global dim FLOCK_AX#(48) `how it was steering, the last time that it was worked out, in pixels a second, every second
global dim FLOCK_AY#(48)
global dim FLOCK_BORN(48) `when it left the board, on the clock of the game. it is not there until then.
global dim FLOCK_FACE(48) `which way it faces: 1 to the right, and -1 to the left
global dim FLOCK_SPRITES(48)
global FLOCK_STEER_NEXT = 0 `the fish that is worked out next
global FLOCK_STEER_EACH = 3 `how many fish are worked out on a frame. with FLOCK_MAX of them, each one is worked out every FLOCK_MAX / FLOCK_STEER_EACH frames.
global dim FLOCK_STEERED(48) `when each one was last worked out, on the clock of the game. the steer is used for all of the time since.
global dim FLOCK_DRAWN(48) `what its sprite has been told: 0 nothing yet, 1 while it is on its way out, and 2 once it is all the way out, after which its size, color and line are left alone
global dim FLOCK_SHOWING(48) `1 while its sprite is showing, so that it is only shown or hidden when that changes
global FLOCK_LOOK_SIG = -1 `what the sliders of the debug panel that change how they look were, the last frame
global FLOCK_LAST_MS = 0

global FLOCK_SIZE = 11 `how big a fish out there is drawn, in pixels. the fish on the board are CELL_ART_SIZE.
global FLOCK_ALPHA = 165 `how much of it can be seen, out there, from 0 to 255
global FLOCK_HAZE_R = 165 `the color that it takes on, which is the blue of the water far off
global FLOCK_HAZE_G = 195
global FLOCK_HAZE_B = 230
global FLOCK_SETTLE_MS = 1800 `how long it takes to swim from the board to out there
global FLOCK_LIFT_SPEED = 26 `how fast a fish swims off of the board, in pixels a second
global FLOCK_SPEED_MIN = 7 `how slowly a fish out there can swim, and how fast, in pixels a second
global FLOCK_SPEED_MAX = 22
global FLOCK_NEAR = 60 `how far away a fish of the same kind can be, and still be swum with, in pixels
global FLOCK_GAP = 14 `how close a fish lets one of its own kind get, in pixels
global FLOCK_AVOID = 46 `how close it lets a fish of another kind get, in pixels
global FLOCK_EDGE = 24 `how far from the edge of the screen it turns back, in pixels
global FLOCK_PULL_COHERE = 30 `how hard it steers toward the middle of the ones near it, in hundredths
global FLOCK_PULL_ALIGN = 50 `how hard it steers to swim the way that they do, in hundredths
global FLOCK_PULL_GAP = 900 `how hard it steers away from one of its own kind that is too close
global FLOCK_PULL_AVOID = 1400 `how hard it steers away from a fish of another kind that is too close
global FLOCK_PULL_HOME = 4 `how hard a fish far from its school steers back to it, in hundredths
global FLOCK_PULL_EDGE = 60 `how hard it steers away from the edge of the screen
global FLOCK_WANDER = 6 `how much it wanders on its own, in pixels a second, every second
global ORDER_FLOCK = -5 `on top of the sea floor, and underneath the coral, the specks and the fish
global FLOCK_FX_ID = 0 `FlockEffect.fx, which fades the line around a fish
global FLOCK_LINE_KEEP = 25 `how much of the line around a fish is left, all the way out, from 0 to 255
global FLOCK_PULL_GRID = 50 `how hard a fish over the board is pushed off of it, in pixels a second, every second
global FLOCK_GRID_MARGIN = 10 `and how far past the edge of the board that starts, in pixels
global FLOCK_GRID_L = 0 `the board, in pixels, worked out on every frame
global FLOCK_GRID_R = 0
global FLOCK_GRID_T = 0
global FLOCK_GRID_B = 0

` THE FANFARE OF THE SCHOOLS. see above.
global SCHOOL_FANFARE_LENGTH = 8 `how many chords a run has
global dim SCHOOL_FANFARE_ROOT(16) `the roots of the chords of the two runs: the one over D minor, and then the one over B flat
global SCHOOL_FANFARE_BIG = 5 `a school this big adds a note on top
global SCHOOL_SONG_AT = 0 `which chord of the run the next school plays
global SCHOOL_SONG_LAST = 0 `when the last school played, on the clock of the game
global SCHOOL_SONG_HEARD = 0 `1 once a school has played in this game
global SCHOOL_SONG_RESET_MS = 60000 `how long it takes with no school for the song to start again from the top
global SCHOOL_CHORD_INSTRUMENT = 0 `INSTRUMENT_BELL. see the instruments in fish_headers.
global SCHOOL_CHORD_VOLUME = 15 `how loud, in hundredths
global SCHOOL_NOTE_GAP = 125 `how far apart the notes of a fanfare are, in milliseconds, from the bottom up
global SCHOOL_NOTE_MAX = 16 `the most notes that a school plays
global dim SCHOOL_CHORD_NOTES(16) `the notes that a school is playing
global dim SCHOOL_CHORD_AT(16) `and when each of them is due, on the clock of the game, or 0 for one that has rung
global SCHOOL_CHORD_PLAYING = 0 `the instrument that they are on

` the fish out in the background turn around, too
global dim FLOCK_SHOWN#(48) `how far around a fish out there is drawn, from 0, the way that its picture faces, to 1, turned around
global FLOCK_TURN_EASE# = 0.005 `how much of the way it turns in a millisecond

` THE SAVED GAME. see above. these are the numbers from SCHOOL_PREF on.
global SCHOOL_PREF = 5000 `1 when the saved game has these
global SCHOOL_PREF_FLOCK = 5001 `how many fish are out in the background, and then one number for each of them
global SCHOOL_PREF_FACES = 5060 `the way that every fish on the board faces, 30 cells to a number
